 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No battle, armies or spoils drawn: geometric for «فأن لله خمسه» and «وإن الله لسميع عليم», mountains for the two sides of the valley. Al-Muyassar's «وخِذْلان أعدائه بالقتل والأسر» is not displayed. STAGING v4: c1 (41): the ruling of the fifth shown in a market by day, with nothing of war: a seal plate for the fifth that belongs to Allah (41:6-8, ending as the Messenger is named); the Prophet's kin and the orphans are not drawn (no children, nobody standing for his family); the believers (a group, never a lone man) hand a purse to a poor man on 41:13 (the needy) and to a traveller on 41:15 (the wayfarer); both raise their hands on 41:30-32, after the condition. 41:16-28 (the condition, the servant to whom it was sent down, the day of the criterion when the two armies met) gets camera only: no battle, no plate starting on the Prophet. A geometric plate for Allah's power (41:29). Every place on stage is occupied, so no pan drifts to an empty side. c2 (42) stays ambient: the two sides of the valley at Badr (battle)."
 },
